{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_012FMHGGs9E4LCLUoMp9Z6FP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nr5Fw9jK2zjzd4qv4pmM7Q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"TODO.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"- [ ] **sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone**\", \"- [x] **sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone**\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> KEY_DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n- **sos_120**: The Paradigm \"copy\" is a shallow copy of the exiled card placed\n  in exile and genuinely *cast* via `cast_spell_free` (fires the cast event —\n  rule 707.12-style copy-cast), rather than a `copy_spell` stack copy, because\n  the original is in exile, not on the stack. A resolved copy ceases to exist\n  (removed from the stack zone, lands nowhere) and never re-registers the\n  recurring trigger (`_is_paradigm_copy` flag). The recurring trigger stays\n  registered for the rest of the game while the original remains in exile.\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"sos_120: Improvisation Capstone\"","description":"Mark sos_120 done, log, commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1804,"cache_read_input_tokens":263909,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1804},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9ba450d-f060-432e-b173-842056ff72e4","uuid":"ec9f185d-1323-4d32-97c2-555dc97f9ad8","request_id":"req_011CbuKM3dLtvuxyeZxxdht4"}
