{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_019boEFyqMfx1Qb3qnRytjxK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WQKDCcXUGqtufByAvvTb2U","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np = \"TODO.md\"\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace(\"- [ ] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares**\",\n              \"- [x] **sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares** *(ETB moved to `on_resolve` — engine fires the ETB event before registering the entering card's own triggers, so a self-ETB trigger never fires; fdn_205 convention)*\")\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> KEY_DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n- **sos_13**: Self-ETB effects can't use `register_triggers` (the engine fires\n  the ETB event before registering the entering card's triggers — fdn_205 puts\n  them in `on_resolve` instead; entries that bypass resolution, e.g.\n  reanimation, miss the effect — engine-wide limitation). The \"more creatures\"\n  count adds +1 for Emeritus itself (still on the stack during on_resolve).\n  Per rule 722.3c the Swords copy is created in exile when it becomes\n  prepared, castable while prepared via the engine's exile-cast path\n  (`cast_spell_free` — unpaid; the engine has no paying cast-from-exile path),\n  unprepares at cast time, and ceases to exist on resolution or when\n  Emeritus leaves/unprepares.\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"sos_13: Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\"","description":"Mark sos_13 done, log, commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_read_input_tokens":286211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9ba450d-f060-432e-b173-842056ff72e4","uuid":